    "The shared BOSH helper is tested with finite in-process ports and actual items/channels/FIFO; no full BoshActor or HTTP dispatch qualification is claimed",
    "Controlled COMMIT futures and returned authority do not prove SQL locking, expiry, atomicity or response-loss fidelity",
    "The post-transfer FIFO-refusal control supplies an already full FIFO to the private continuation after a controlled transfer; it does not prove a concurrent production FIFO change at that synchronous boundary",
    "Notification_attempted is separate from actual one-shot delivery, queue acceptance and durable settlement",
    "The logical transfer-record bound follows the existing actor flow; additional lazy Vec/Arc metadata is outside XML governor accounting, and no numeric capacity/RSS ceiling is claimed",
    "validate_for_io checks pre-I/O state but does not consume a start permit; the actual private helper makes one port call, and enter_commit admits one COMMIT",
    "The SM guard hardens inconsistent adapter results; existing SQL emits typed supersession before COMMIT, and no production SQL defect was demonstrated",
    "BOSH response bind/rebuild/exposure/cache/renewal/ACK, shared direct continuation, composed replay/mutation/shrinking and full Stage3 acceptance remain open",
